 import:","+The root `index.ts` wires runtime dependencies and passes them to the","+implementation. Dependency rules apply to every service, regardless of its","+`migrated` marker or presence in the inventory. Implementation files may import:"," ","-- Files within the same service, except its root `index.ts`.","+- Files within the same service, except its root `index.ts` or `index.js`."," - Types, using explicit type-only imports."," - The libraries and individual shared files in the","   [dependency-cruiser config](../../../../.dependency-cruiser.cjs).","@@ -143,7 +145,7 @@ root is fine, including validating configuration with Zod and passing computed"," values such as `getUnixTime()`."," "," `pnpm lint:oxlint` enforces direct constructor wiring with","-`ghost/no-injected-service-libraries`. In migrated root `index.ts` files, it","+`ghost/no-injected-service-libraries`. In root `index.ts` files, it"," rejects allowlisted imports and `const require()` bindings passed to constructors"," imported from within that service, including values in literal options objects"," and arrays. It reads the same allowlist and service scope as the boundary rule.","@@ -154,7 +156,9 @@ Logging, config, settings, models, event buses and other service instances"," belong in the root wiring. Nested `index.ts` files are implementation files, not"," extra wiring roots. The rule covers static imports, `require()`, literal dynamic"," imports and re-exports. All implementation source inside a service is checked, including","-nested folders named `test` or `fixtures`.","+nested folders named `test` or `fixtures`. The scan cannot follow a computed","+`require()` or `import()` argument, so `import/no-dynamic-require` rejects those","+in every service file."," "," Some dependencies look like libraries but are treated as instances:"," ","@@ -197,10 +201,41 @@ adjacent `build:tsc` output out of the report; ordinary JavaScript implementatio"," remain checked. Package exports resolve through their `source` condition when"," available, so workspace contracts are checked without relying on build output."," ","-`pnpm lint:boundaries`, also run by `pnpm check` and CI, enforces these rules as","-errors for every entry marked `migrated: true`. New implementation files inherit","-the same rules. Marking a service migrated opts it into enforcement; review","-changes to that marker as part of the migration.","+`pnpm lint:boundaries`, also run by `pnpm check` and CI, checks all service","+implementations in the same dependency-cruiser scan as Core and app boundaries.","+Top-level `index.ts` and legacy `index.js` files are wiring roots and exempt;","+nested indexes and standalone service files are checked. This preserves the","+legacy audit's wiring exemption without making migration status an enforcement","+switch.","+","+Existing violations are recorded in","+[the known-violations file](../../../../.dependency-cruiser-known-violations.json).","+Each entry names one rule, importing file and dependency. External packages use","+the exact import specifier, including subpaths, so pnpm store locations do not","+change the baseline. Local and workspace dependencies use resolved source paths.","+Moving either file or adding a new import cannot inherit another entry's exception.","+","+CI rejects new violations, stale entries, duplicate entries and entries for","+migrated services. When fixing a violation, remove its entry in the same change;","+when marking a service migrated, remove all its entries. Do not regenerate the","+file to accept new violations. The file should only shrink. Any exceptional","+addition or move needs explicit review; CODEOWNERS covers it and the rule config.","+","+A few unmigrated services change too often for a file-level list to hold: it","+would go stale between a pull request opening and merging. The checker's","+[`deferredServices`](../../../../tools/scripts/lib/dependency-boundaries.ts) list","+names them. Their violations stay in reports and in the lint summary count, but","+do not fail lint and have no entries in the file. In those services, still pass","+new dependencies in through whatever file already composes the service. A","+service leaves the list when it is migrated. The list should only shrink, and a","+service that is not named is checked from its first commit.","+","+The shared [boundary checker](../../../../tools/scripts/lib/dependency-boundaries.ts)","+compares the current graph with this file. Native dependency-cruiser baselines","+match resolved paths and silently retain stale entries, so they cannot enforce","+this contract on their own. `gx services report` and `gx services audit` use the","+same scan and file, retaining all current findings so migration reports still","+show the remaining work."," "," The allowlist names individual packages or files, with a reason for each."," Review additions individually; do not allow whole shared directories or all"],"additions":45,"deletions":10,"truncated":false},{"path":"ghost/core/server/services/comments/comments-service-email-renderer.js","lines":["@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ class CommentsServiceEmailRenderer {","   async renderEmailTemplate(templateName, data) {","     const htmlTemplateSource = await this.readTemplate(templateName);"],"additions":0,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":1827,"deletions":31,"truncated":true,"file_count":6},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-12T17:12:50.755821+00:00"}